Chicago95 on openSUSE (home:caiocco)
====================================

Upstream: https://github.com/grassmunk/Chicago95

What is left out
----------------
The source tarball is repacked by prune-microsoft-assets.sh (in the
source package). It removes every upstream file that reproduces
Microsoft artwork. The list follows Clay Risser's Debian packaging
(chicago95 3.0.1+git20260803.e89583c+ds-1, debian/copyright
Files-Excluded):

 - the Windows 95 Plymouth boot splash (Plymouth/Chicago95)
 - the stock wallpapers and pattern tiles, Extras/setup.png
 - the Windows 95 startup recording and the event sounds (DING, TADA,
   CHORD...), so there is no sound theme or login sound
 - Office (Word/Excel/PowerPoint/Access), MSN, MS-DOS executable,
   Internet Explorer and "My Computer" icons, plus every byte-identical
   copy of them under other names (terminal, menu, desktop, internet...)
 - the Windows-flag Start button images and start-here/distributor-logo
   icons of the "Chicago95" icon theme
 - Plus/ (the Plus! theme converter), which ships Microsoft icons and
   screenshots of third-party themes

The freed names point at icons the theme keeps:
 - office document/spreadsheet/presentation/database -> text-x-generic
 - application-x-ms-dos-executable -> application-x-executable
 - web browser names -> firefox
 - computer -> computer-laptop
 - start-here, distributor-logo and the Xfce menu-button icons in
   "Chicago95" -> the Tux start-here of Chicago95-tux
Other aliases of removed icons are gone; their lookup falls back to the
inherited icon theme.

Not packaged either: the LightDM webkit greeter theme, the KDE/SDDM
themes, installer.py (per-user GUI installer) and Extras/ files meant for
manual setup (Firefox/ScummVM/LibreOffice add-ons, Qt and compton
configs, shell prompts). They are in the upstream repo.

Setting it up in Xfce
---------------------
 - Settings > Appearance: Style "Chicago95", Icons "Chicago95-tux"
   (or Chicago95 / Chicago95-puffy)
 - Settings > Window Manager: Theme "Chicago95"
 - Settings > Mouse and Touchpad > Theme: e.g. Chicago95_Cursor_White
 - xfce4-terminal: Preferences > Colors > Presets "Chicago95"
 - xfce4-panel-profiles: the "Chicago95_Panel_Preferences" layout
 - Plymouth (package plymouth-theme-chicago95-retrotux):
     sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -R RetroTux

Upstream's INSTALL.md has the full guide; the original UI font (MS Sans
Serif) is proprietary and not included.

Licenses
--------
Themes, icons, cursors, RetroTux: GPL-3.0-or-later OR MIT (upstream
README; theme files carry "License: GPL-3.0+").
Chicago95-puffy pixel-art variations: CC-BY-SA-4.0 (Puffy is owned by
the OpenBSD group).
Cronyx Cyrillic bitmap fonts: Cronyx license ("may be used, modified,
copied, distributed, and sold, in both source and binary form provided
that the above copyright and these terms are retained").
Perfect DOS VGA 437 (Zeh Fernando) / Less/More Perfect DOS VGA
(laemeur): public domain.
